        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trudge/{size}/2062_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-07-02T09:01:31.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So, I saw a rumor (well, wild speculation really) that one of the upcoming decks would be multiple heroes.</p><p>If that's true, I think it will be Miss Information's nemesis.&nbsp; Specifically, I think Miss Information's nemesis is a bunch of kid superheroes (or sidekicks)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I have a few reasons for thinking this:</p><p>1) Miss Information's nemesis symbols is a pair of brackets, which in math is used to denote a set.</p><p>2) Much of Miss Information's danger comes from the fact that the Freedom Five don't see her as a threat.&nbsp; I think children are more likely to catch on, even if the adult heroes don't take the kids' warnings seriously.</p><p>3) A lot of Miss Information's cards have very basic sounding threats (old lady in the street, cat in the tree).&nbsp; That sounds less like a job for Bunker, and more of a job for lil'turret (or, you know, whatever his kid version would be).</p><p>4) Of the various four-color superhero tropes we've seen so far, the kid sidekick or scrappy kid hero has been missing.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>But this might be wishful thinking on my part, and really wanting to see a hero deck with Ennead-like mechanics.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:38:45.812Z",
