        "id": 66911,
        "name": "Ameena",
        "username": "Ameena",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-07-02T10:08:56.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I wonder how that'd work…a deck with multiple heroes. More people to get hit by stuff, I suppose…but more people to do damage? I suppose they'd have to have less hp in order to balance things out, just as the Ennead have much less health relative to all the other villains. If that were the case, I think a game versus Iron Legacy would be even shorter than usual, lol.</p>\n<p>Hey, if there were some child heroes, maybe one of them would be Thiago (the Potential Sidekick from Spite's deck) - he'd seem an obvious choice, at least. Though from what I can tell, he's not a superhero but just a boy who dresses up like Legacy because he wants to <span class=\"bbcode-i\">be</span> a superhero. Hopefully he's nothing like Buddy from \"The Incredibles\" ;).</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:44:45.146Z",
