        "created_at": "2013-07-02T18:23:09.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"trudge\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trudge/48/2062_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> trudge:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Of the various four-color superhero tropes we've seen so far, the kid sidekick or scrappy kid hero has been missing.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Don't we already have Unity?</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ameena\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/48/1907_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ameena:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I wonder how that'd work…a deck with multiple heroes. More people to get hit by stuff, I suppose…but more people to do damage? I suppose they'd have to have less hp in order to balance things out, just as the Ennead have much less health relative to all the other villains. If that were the case, I think a game versus Iron Legacy would be even shorter than usual, lol.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Don't we already have Unity?</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Hey, if there were some child heroes, maybe one of them would be Thiago (the Potential Sidekick from Spite's deck) - he'd seem an obvious choice, at least. Though from what I can tell, he's not a superhero but just a boy who dresses up like Legacy because he wants to   be   a superhero. Hopefully he's nothing like Buddy from \"The Incredibles\" ;).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I always forget that we actually know Potential Sidekick's name, since I always just call him Schroedinger Boy (he might be dead, might be alive, might be Wraith's sidekick, might be someone else's, etc).</p>\n<p>As far as gedgeteer sidekicks who turn into future villains go, well, we&nbsp;<em>do</em> already have Unity…</p>\n<p>Ironic</p>",
